---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/paths';
---

<Layout title="Privacy" description="What the submission form collects and how it is handled. Emails are never published.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>

    <h2>What the submission form collects</h2>
    <p>The <a href={url('submit/')}>submission form</a> asks for these things and nothing else:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which facility it is about, or "new facility"</li>
      <li>The type of submission: document, meeting notice, news article, correction or tip</li>
      <li>A link or an uploaded file</li>
      <li>The date of the thing you are sending</li>
      <li>Short notes</li>
      <li>Your email address, only if you choose to give it</li>
      <li>A checkbox for whether we may contact you about this submission</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you open the form from a facility page, the facility is filled in for you. The form service also records the
      date and time you sent it.
    </p>

    <h2>Emails are never published</h2>
    <p>
      Your email address is never published on this site or anywhere else. We use it only to contact you about your
      submission, and only if you checked the box.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing you send goes on the site until we review it. If we use it, we cite the document or article itself. We
      do not name you.
    </p>

    <h2>Where submissions are stored</h2>
    <p>
      Submissions are stored in Tally, the form service this site uses. Only the maintainer of this site reviews them.
      <a href="https://tally.so/help/privacy-policy">Tally's privacy policy</a> covers how Tally stores data.
    </p>

    <h2>Deleting a submission</h2>
    <p>
      To have a submission deleted, send a new submission with the type "correction." Put "delete my submission" in
      the notes and give the email address you used before, if you gave one. We will delete it from Tally.
    </p>

    <h2>The rest of the site</h2>
    <p>
      This site has no accounts. It sets no cookies of its own and uses no analytics. The map images are loaded from
      OpenStreetMap's servers and the form is loaded from Tally. Like any website, those services can see your IP
      address when your browser loads them.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
